      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Input Validation-Server Side:\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Input Validation-Server Side:\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FXp6HNb3Q35r6ZjF3-QD1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 363.8246514415448,
      "y": -189.4884898041468,
      "width": 1465.19921875,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bcV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1880676370,
      "version": 642,
      "versionNonce": 726789330,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730624086220,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "All right everyone now let's dive into How we can do server side \ninput validation ,that is if we have a form that username and email\nid as input than we should validate the field value if username.isString()\nand email.isEmail() to give back a boolean value cause user can enter \nnumber in email field which is not our server is designed to handle \n\nso to avoid  any error we do input validation so that server respond with \ncorrect data and avoid running into any error",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "All right everyone now let's dive into How we can do server side \ninput validation ,that is if we have a form that username and email\nid as input than we should validate the field value if username.isString()\nand email.isEmail() to give back a boolean value cause user can enter \nnumber in email field which is not our server is designed to handle \n\nso to avoid  any error we do input validation so that server respond with \ncorrect data and avoid running into any error",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TS3Iqg9VDMxKNCUj33VVw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 378.64505399094287,
      "y": 276.42500599852485,
      "width": 1445.5989990234375,
      "height": 270,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bcW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 340428306,
      "version": 185,
      "versionNonce": 1992374798,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730624168613,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So there are two validation middleware or 3rd party module we primary use\n1.express-validator\n2.zod\n\nWe will start with express-validator:\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So there are two validation middleware or 3rd party module we primary use\n1.express-validator\n2.zod\n\nWe will start with express-validator:\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2L8McwXjwEO5KANGR1iyJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 342.81037068037267,
      "y": 664.0549176596,
      "width": 2177.998779296875,
      "height": 180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bcZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1410511502,
      "version": 59,
      "versionNonce": 1533756046,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730640504497,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Input validation in Express is crucial for ensuring that the data received from users is correct, secure, \nand meets the expected criteria. It helps prevent issues such as SQL injection, XSS attacks, and ensures that \nyour application behaves as intended. Here’s a detailed guide on how to implement input validation in \nan Express application using libraries like Express Validator and Zod.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Input validation in Express is crucial for ensuring that the data received from users is correct, secure, \nand meets the expected criteria. It helps prevent issues such as SQL injection, XSS attacks, and ensures that \nyour application behaves as intended. Here’s a detailed guide on how to implement input validation in \nan Express application using libraries like Express Validator and Zod.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "zyxrnQ9mxo-m0_ng2yo_r",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 361.1036189138938,
      "y": 1005.2211868368322,
      "width": 2692.798583984375,
      "height": 585,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bca",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1885627726,
      "version": 16,
      "versionNonce": 1121051858,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730640543719,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Input Validation Basics\nInput validation involves checking the data submitted by users (typically through forms) to ensure it adheres to certain rules, such as:\n\n->Required fields must not be empty.\n->Data types must match expectations (e.g., strings, numbers).\n->Data must conform to specific formats (e.g., email addresses).\n->Values must be within a specific range or set of values.\n\n2. Using Express Validator\nExpress Validator is a popular middleware for validating and sanitizing user inputs in Express.\n\nInstallation\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Input Validation Basics\nInput validation involves checking the data submitted by users (typically through forms) to ensure it adheres to certain rules, such as:\n\n->Required fields must not be empty.\n->Data types must match expectations (e.g., strings, numbers).\n->Data must conform to specific formats (e.g., email addresses).\n->Values must be within a specific range or set of values.\n\n2. Using Express Validator\nExpress Validator is a popular middleware for validating and sanitizing user inputs in Express.\n\nInstallation\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
